name verbatlas-preference-info
# README.txt, PACKAGE CONTENTS, names the file VA_preference_info.tsv "(name, id, reference synset for each preference)".
# README.txt, FORMAT, describes it under the name "5. VA_preference_ids.tsv":
#   "Each line contains the ID of a VerbAtlas selectional preference, its reference
#    BabelNet synset ID, and its name."
# The predicates are the README's names for the second and third columns. The names after "columns" only point at a
# position in the row and are never recorded, except "name", which "attest" records as the README writes it.
# The file has a fourth column the README does not describe or name. It is recorded as a pair, the row's ID and the
# field, in the row's own order.
# The file's first line is a licence line ("VerbAtlas 1.1.0 - SapienzaNLP - LICENSE: ..."), not a row.
match VA_preference_info.tsv
grammar table
comment V
columns ID reference_BabelNet_synset_ID name fourth

claims
predicate reference BabelNet synset ID
subject in ID
object in reference_BabelNet_synset_ID

claims
subject in ID
attest name

claims
pair
subject in ID
object in fourth
